\label{lem:affine-inversion-continuous}



The map $A \mapsto A^{-1}$ is continuous on $\mathrm{Aff}^+_{\mathbb{R}}$.
In particular, inversion defines a homeomorphism of $\mathrm{Aff}^+_{\mathbb{R}}$ to itself.

